WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.200
Can.

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.734
The Ukrainian

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:02.202
Air Force tonight is falling

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.003
just short

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.870
of claiming

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.005
official responsibility

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.007
for yet another drone strike

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.441
deep inside Russian territory.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.642
But they're certainly not denying

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.377
it either.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.878
A spokesperson for the Air Force

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.046
Air Force saying, quote,

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.247
This is just a consequence

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.281
of what Russia is doing,

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.250
which is the relentless bombardment

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.451
of civilian infrastructure

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.386
targets that cause

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:20.186
rolling blackouts

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.388
affecting millions of people

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:22.288
across this country

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.356
in the dead of winter.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.425
Now, as far as this latest drone strike

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:26.793
in the western port city of Engels,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.261
which is along the Volga River

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.330
around 500 miles southeast of Moscow,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.164
we know that at least

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.298
three Russian servicemen

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:33.266
were killed on Monday.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.234
And we also know

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.535
this is the second attempted

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.237
drone attack on this area,

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.572
which includes a strategic bomber airbase

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.007
Now, Russian state media is claiming

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.142
that this drone was shot down.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:43.376
We cannot independently verify

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:44.244
that claim.

00:00:44.244 --> 00:00:45.545
Meanwhile, in Moscow,

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.213
President Putin is

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:47.914
well, he's certainly

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:48.948
getting a lot of skepticism,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.816
not just here in Ukraine,

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.851
but around the world for his offer

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.619
that is believed here

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.721
in Ukraine to be disingenuous,

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.290
to negotiate to an end to this war, talk

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.592
about acceptable solutions in his words.

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.361
Adviser to President

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.363
Zelensky says that Moscow

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.564
doesn't really want to negotiate.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.032
They just want to avoid responsibility

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.267
for their continuing

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.435
attacks on civilians,

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.936
that Ukraine says warrants them

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.305
being kicked out of the United Nations

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.907
and the United Nations Security Council,

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.475
where they're a permanent member

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:17.877
with veto power, one of five.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.445
There's actually no

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.079
mechanism written

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.580
into the UN Charter to remove them.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.782
So that is more of a political statement

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:25.185
than an actual possibility at this stage,

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.820
although the Ukrainians

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.420
would certainly like

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.022
to see some consequences at the U.N.

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:29.456
for Russia,

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:30.190
because essentially

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:30.723
they have the power

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.093
to veto any resolutions against them.

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.360
Meanwhile, here in Kiev,

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.495
President Alinsky

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:36.896
calling for patience

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:37.263
and faith

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.264
from the Ukrainian people

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.132
and warning that there could be

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.301
some difficult and dark days ahead.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.902
When he gave his Christmas address,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.671
he warned of the potential

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.372
of Russian retaliation.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:46.773
Of course,

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.041
he didn't mention the drone strike,

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:48.842
but in general,

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.577
the Ukrainians are worried

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:51.044
that there could be

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.445
some sort of major Russian attack

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.947
before the end of the year

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.282
after a brief pause over Christmas.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.084
And Dmitri Medvedev

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.186
the former president of Ukraine,

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.754
he is saying that Russia

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.123
will engage in this war

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.390
until, quote, the disgusting,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.291
almost fascist

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:05.892
regime in

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.560
Kiev is both removed

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.661
and demilitarize eyes,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.796
which certainly is very different

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.730
language from President

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:11.865
Putin saying he's

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.800
willing to negotiate power.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:14.567
All right, Will Ripley,

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.368
thank you so much.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.202
And more perspective now

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.971
from CNN military analyst

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:18.705
and retired Army

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:20.507
Lieutenant General Mark Hertling.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.474
General Hertling.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.208
You heard that report

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.676
there from Will Ripley.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:24.611
What is your reaction

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.546
to this new strike on an air base

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.515
deep inside Russian territory?

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:30.750
Let's call it what

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.351
it is, Pam

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.153
Angles to air base

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.287
near the city of Sacra,

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.922
about 400 kilometers away

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.990
from the front line,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.790
has several

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.059
important factors regarding its.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.427
This has been an effective

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.362
operational target

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:45.398
now twice for the Ukrainian military.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.099
And it's important

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.133
for about four reasons.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.635
First, it shows Russia

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.270
they have no safe haven

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.172
and they must defend their facilities

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.339
wherever they are.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:53.907
Secondly,

00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:56.042
it shows Ukraine has a strike capability

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.810
that Russia didn't know about Third,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.179
and most importantly

00:02:59.179 --> 00:02:59.946
and goes to

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.849
is the base for the T u one 60 aircraft.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:03.950
That's something called

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.151
the backfire bomber.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.386
And that airplane

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.454
has a standoff capability and

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.224
it's able to launch

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.126
multiple cruise missiles.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.127
These are the missiles

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:14.827
that have been launched

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.963
from outside the territory of Ukraine

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.265
to affect the infrastructure

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.500
within Ukraine.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.135
And that's why Ukraine is targeting.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.170
But finally, the most important part.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.271
There is reports tonight

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.407
that these aircraft have now been moved

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.543
further to the east and Russia 4000

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.011
miles away from the

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.780
from the Ukrainian border.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.181
That's three time zones.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:37.250
And if so, it will require Russia

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.718
to launch those aircraft,

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.220
use a lot more fuel

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.754
and be able to be picked up.

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.756
So it's they're all critically important.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.159
So that is the practical military effect.

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.594
Meantime, you have Vladimir Putin

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.195
saying on Sunday

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.463
that he is ready to, quote,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.332
negotiate with everyone involved

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.066
in this process

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.134
about acceptable solutions, end quote.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.869
With regard to the war in Ukraine.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.571
You have actually,

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.339
what should we say,

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.841
quote, negotiated with Russians.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.010
What did that experience tell you

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.679
about Putin's intentions here?

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:07.146
Yeah, well,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.349
I certainly haven't negotiated with Mr.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.083
Putin himself,

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:10.950
but I have

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.253
negotiated with some of his military

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.554
officers, his generals

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:15.588
and some of his Ministry

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.723
of Defense officials.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.091
And what I will tell you is this.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.993
I learned valuable lessons, Pamela.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.928
First of all, they lie.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:22.862
Secondly,

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.631
they will never negotiate

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.199
evenly And thirdly,

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:27.900
if they do finally negotiate

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.302
and you think you have a deal,

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.070
they will renege on that deal.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.672
And what's important about this,

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.541
all of our European allies know this.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.743
And it seems

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.811
the Americans are slow to learn this,

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.313
that it's just not a good thing

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.881
to negotiate with Putin,

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.950
because he lies, he detracts

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.352
and he reneges on any deal that he makes.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.421
Ukraine, as we as well

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:48.855
pointed out,

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.189
is calling for Russia

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.025
to be excluded from the U.N..

00:04:52.025 --> 00:04:52.892
What do you make of that?

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:54.727
Yeah, I'm

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:54.961
not going

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.396
to comment on that

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.297
because that's something

00:04:57.297 --> 00:04:58.831
for the politicians to decide.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.000
But I've also seen reports from

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.335
from CNN reporters

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:02.769
saying that's

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:05.772
going to be very difficult to do because

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:07.573
the Soviet Union, not Russia,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:08.508
the Soviet Union

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:10.143
was one of the founding members

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.010
of the U.N.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:11.878
and because of

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:15.114
that was one of the five original members

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:15.915
that makes up that.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:17.350
But it's going to be tough

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.284
to kick them off

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.653
because they have a veto vote.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.821
They can just veto anybody

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:22.822
that tries to kick them off

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:23.823
that Security Council.

